# This file is committed to the repo on purpose (normally .env.local is
# gitignored). Solo consultant, single-user MVP, no paying customers yet —
# the friction of a non-technical collaborator wiring up their own Supabase
# credentials outweighed the risk. Two things make this a smaller risk than
# it looks:
#   1. Both values below are Vite `VITE_` vars, which means they're already
#      inlined into the built JS bundle and shipped to every browser that
#      loads the app — committing them to git doesn't expose anything that
#      wasn't already public in the deployed site.
#   2. VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY is Supabase's "publishable" key, designed to
#      be public; it's meant to be constrained by Row Level Security, not
#      secrecy.
# What this does NOT cover: the schema currently has no RLS policies (see
# db/schema.sql), so anyone with this URL + key can read/write the database
# directly. Revisit this the moment there's a paying customer, real user
# data at stake, or the repo goes public — rotate the key in the Supabase
# dashboard and stop committing this file.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://xeqbgtjtorvcphymfjxs.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_IqPpDwTtA6YrF9erDJGkHQ_p_2Zc2sH
